WEBVTT

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:22.189
So, we can finally make good use
of the asset we picked up in the old town.

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:26.860
<i>Leon, I'm ready.</i>

00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:28.195
O-- Okay.

00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:31.990
Now activating the Dark Drive.

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:35.202
Queenie, please begin.

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:37.454
Activating Dark Drive.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:42.709
How is it?

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:49.341
Emergency shutdown!

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:53.595
It won't start.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:57.849
Then I guess the activation factor is
different than the hyperdrive after all.

00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:01.019
The hyperdrive requires the presence
of a human being.

00:01:01.812 --> 00:01:03.939
What does the Dark Drive require?

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:37.407
Out of the way!

00:02:37.866 --> 00:02:38.700
Huh?

00:02:39.076 --> 00:02:39.910
Dr. Lon Woo

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:43.997
Is the mahua stand
that's always next to you closed today?

00:02:45.457 --> 00:02:49.252
No, they shut down. I heard they weren't
able to get flour anymore.

00:02:49.544 --> 00:02:52.422
The BRAI attacks have been
pretty bad recently.

00:02:52.881 --> 00:02:55.008
Goods from other towns
just stopped arriving.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:58.970
Let's see if there are any other shops
that sell mahua.

00:03:02.557 --> 00:03:05.936
So, the basic makeup and principles
are roughly the same?

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:08.897
<i>It's likely</i>
<i>that the ignition factor is different.</i>

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.650
Wasn't one of the ignition factors
for the hyperdrive

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:13.402
the presence of a human being?

00:03:13.735 --> 00:03:17.864
<i>Right, so Doug, Queenie, and I</i>
<i>tested it out.</i>

00:03:18.323 --> 00:03:20.117
I haven't tried it yet!

00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:22.953
You're not getting a turn, Sarge.

00:03:23.078 --> 00:03:24.996
It's Captain, not Sarge!

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:25.914
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:26.123 --> 00:03:28.875
It's possible the Dark Drive's
ignition factor is...

00:03:29.418 --> 00:03:30.419
BRAI.

00:03:30.502 --> 00:03:32.838
<i>Yes, I'd say that's likely.</i>

00:03:33.422 --> 00:03:35.173
Little sis, here's some booze.

00:03:35.257 --> 00:03:38.009
It's Chloe! I'm still working.

00:03:38.844 --> 00:03:40.345
<i>I don't really understand it,</i>

00:03:40.595 --> 00:03:43.807
<i>but the Dark Drive and hyperdrive</i>
<i>mechanisms seem to be similar.</i>

00:03:44.558 --> 00:03:45.475
Yes.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:48.311
And you're a genius, right?

00:03:48.854 --> 00:03:49.938
Huh?

00:03:50.021 --> 00:03:51.356
<i>I see.</i>

00:03:51.732 --> 00:03:55.902
<i>You're saying there's no one else but</i>
<i>Mr. Scientist who could've made it.</i>

00:03:56.486 --> 00:04:00.365
That means there may be someone
helping Gold.

00:04:01.199 --> 00:04:02.075
But who?

00:04:02.951 --> 00:04:05.537
The world of scholars isn't that vast.

00:04:06.163 --> 00:04:10.917
It's a possibility that someone you know
made the Dark Drive.

00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:16.757
But can two things so similar
really have been made at the same time?

00:04:18.967 --> 00:04:19.968
Leon...

00:04:22.888 --> 00:04:24.890
There have been instances of

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.768
important inventions
and discoveries being made

00:04:27.851 --> 00:04:29.394
simultaneously across the world.

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.272
Entanglement...

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.692
There must be some connection
between the parallel worlds.

00:04:36.985 --> 00:04:39.279
<i>I've got a few more things</i>
<i>I'd like to test.</i>

00:04:39.529 --> 00:04:41.990
If you find out anything,
notify us immediately.

00:04:42.199 --> 00:04:43.325
<i>Got it. Bye.</i>

00:04:46.203 --> 00:04:48.955
It seems as though Leon Lau is doing well

00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:50.874
as a member of the team.

00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:52.417
Yes...

00:04:55.629 --> 00:04:59.549
I suppose he is a bit more respectable,
compared to how he was.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.805
I'm relieved he seems to be
getting along well.

00:05:05.472 --> 00:05:08.725
He's horrible at working or living
with others.

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:12.479
He's not only bad at small talk,
he doesn't remember names, faces,

00:05:12.562 --> 00:05:16.775
or anything else he's not interested in.
He's unbelievably bumbly.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.610
That's pretty bad.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:22.155
I don't think you're much different,
miss soldier.

00:05:23.198 --> 00:05:24.658
Well, in any case,

00:05:24.741 --> 00:05:27.202
compared to when we first started
living together,

00:05:27.285 --> 00:05:29.412
I think he's made quite a lot of progress.

00:05:34.042 --> 00:05:37.128
Someone who can create a Dark Drive...

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:40.090
8 YEARS AGO

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:44.594
I don't think you've spoken a single word
to anyone since you've been here.

00:05:46.805 --> 00:05:50.267
"There's no one here who functions
on the same level as me."

00:05:52.102 --> 00:05:55.105
That's what you're thinking, right?
Can you play chess?

00:05:55.438 --> 00:05:58.024
If you win, just go on living
as you have been.

00:05:58.567 --> 00:06:00.986
If I win, I want you to do as I say.

00:06:01.444 --> 00:06:02.487
How about it?

00:06:03.238 --> 00:06:05.031
I've never lost a game of chess.

00:06:06.408 --> 00:06:07.617
Even better.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:17.877
Checkmate.

00:06:19.129 --> 00:06:21.339
I'm sensing some shock
from that expression.

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.675
Shall we try a different game?

00:06:24.551 --> 00:06:25.385
Check.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.015
Thirteen orphans.

00:06:37.147 --> 00:06:38.481
The world is a big place.

00:06:38.857 --> 00:06:40.775
There are people that surpass you here.

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:43.236
There are ones that surpass me as well.

00:06:43.945 --> 00:06:46.156
However, you will continue to improve.

00:06:47.032 --> 00:06:48.491
That's why I recruited you.

00:06:49.826 --> 00:06:50.952
Let me introduce myself.

00:06:51.703 --> 00:06:54.497
I'm the leader of
this quantum reactor laboratory,

00:06:54.831 --> 00:06:55.832
Lon Woo.

00:06:58.835 --> 00:07:00.503
Dr. Lon Woo...

00:07:01.338 --> 00:07:03.423
Our academic conference
took a little while.

00:07:04.174 --> 00:07:06.468
I apologize for the late introduction.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:10.055
I read your quantum reactor thesis.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:13.975
Regarding the interpretation
of the multidimensional equation--

00:07:14.726 --> 00:07:16.353
Don't be in such a rush.

00:07:16.978 --> 00:07:20.065
You did promise you'd do whatever I asked.

00:07:20.732 --> 00:07:21.566
Huh?

00:07:44.047 --> 00:07:46.049
The only thing I'm bad at is swimming.

00:07:46.841 --> 00:07:49.719
But I really thought
I could handle it today.

00:07:50.178 --> 00:07:51.262
On what grounds?

00:07:52.013 --> 00:07:53.223
Just my intuition.

00:07:55.892 --> 00:07:57.394
Just look at these fringes.

00:07:57.894 --> 00:08:02.357
How much experimentation went into these
before this shape was settled on?

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.027
"Why am I doing such pointless things?"

00:08:06.528 --> 00:08:09.990
"I thought I would learn something
by doing things with him."

00:08:10.907 --> 00:08:12.492
Is what you're thinking, right?

00:08:14.995 --> 00:08:17.414
I work only eight hours a day.

00:08:18.415 --> 00:08:20.041
I have two days off a week.

00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:25.630
It's my policy to properly enjoy dining,
sports, and even women on occasion.

00:08:27.382 --> 00:08:30.343
You want to use
all of your time for research.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:31.594
Yes.

00:08:31.886 --> 00:08:34.305
And yet, I still surpass you.

00:08:38.977 --> 00:08:42.689
You try to solve every problem you face
with your brain alone.

00:08:43.398 --> 00:08:45.608
Your body and mind are not separate.

00:08:46.568 --> 00:08:49.571
By making changes in your body,
surroundings, and habits,

00:08:49.779 --> 00:08:52.991
you can make changes in your intellect
as well, don't you think?

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.994
I won't know unless I try.

00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:58.538
Then try it.

00:08:58.747 --> 00:09:01.624
Make changes to your body and lifestyle.

00:09:03.585 --> 00:09:06.254
You may see things in a new light.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:08.089
This too, is science.

00:09:08.339 --> 00:09:09.883
-Science?
-Right.

00:09:10.425 --> 00:09:14.471
Why not experiment as a scientist
to verify whether it works?

00:09:14.846 --> 00:09:15.889
If even then

00:09:15.972 --> 00:09:18.933
you disagree with my way of thinking,
I won't complain.

00:09:19.267 --> 00:09:23.480
Is this another one of the things
I have to do for you?

00:09:24.564 --> 00:09:25.899
I won't force you.

00:09:27.358 --> 00:09:28.943
It's your choice.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.585
<i>He's having lunch?</i>

00:09:45.668 --> 00:09:48.046
<i>Yeah, he's started eating with the others.</i>

00:09:48.379 --> 00:09:50.590
<i>He doesn't talk with anyone though.</i>

00:09:51.591 --> 00:09:55.011
<i>His research efficiency and concentration</i>
<i>seem to be increasing.</i>

00:09:56.721 --> 00:09:58.223
<i>You seem to be doing well.</i>

00:09:58.723 --> 00:10:03.603
<i>It does feel as though my mind and vision</i>
<i>are clearer than before.</i>

00:10:04.145 --> 00:10:05.271
<i>That's great.</i>

00:10:06.773 --> 00:10:09.109
There's something I realized
about the reactor.

00:10:10.151 --> 00:10:14.030
The range in quantum tremor fluctuations
is far greater than what's theorized.

00:10:15.031 --> 00:10:17.742
Perhaps something is happening
in the reactor's core.

00:10:19.035 --> 00:10:20.912
You're the first person to notice.

00:10:21.371 --> 00:10:22.622
Then, it's as I thought?

00:10:23.373 --> 00:10:25.083
Using the formula that was published,

00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:28.211
it's impossible to acquire
multidimensional energy.

00:10:28.545 --> 00:10:29.754
Then why would you even...

00:10:30.964 --> 00:10:34.259
At present,
mankind could never understand it.

00:10:35.218 --> 00:10:39.514
It's better to just activate it
so they can see it with their own eyes.

00:10:41.391 --> 00:10:45.895
However, you might arrive at the truth
on your own before then.

00:10:48.481 --> 00:10:51.151
We'll be able to utilize it
sooner than we anticipated.

00:10:51.526 --> 00:10:54.070
Trial vehicle development
is also progressing.

00:10:54.445 --> 00:10:58.575
Everything is on track.
All because you're here now, Leon.

00:11:00.034 --> 00:11:01.035
Excuse me.

00:11:03.288 --> 00:11:04.289
What is it?

00:11:08.251 --> 00:11:11.379
If the ignition factor
for the Dark Drive is BRAI, then...

00:11:11.838 --> 00:11:12.755
Leon.

00:11:12.839 --> 00:11:13.673
Huh?

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:16.843
Are you free after work tomorrow?

00:11:16.968 --> 00:11:18.678
As long as there aren't any problems.

00:11:18.845 --> 00:11:19.679
Why?

00:11:20.179 --> 00:11:21.347
There's...

00:11:21.639 --> 00:11:23.474
somewhere I want to go.

00:11:25.351 --> 00:11:27.103
"Dr. Lon Woo."

00:11:30.064 --> 00:11:31.900
Where should I put this?

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.068
Over in that corner, please.

00:11:34.277 --> 00:11:35.278
Okay!

00:11:37.238 --> 00:11:39.699
Gren, have you seen Leon?

00:11:39.866 --> 00:11:41.868
He left with the Secretary earlier.

00:11:42.368 --> 00:11:43.578
With Jay?

00:11:45.288 --> 00:11:47.123
Why did you bring me here?

00:11:48.124 --> 00:11:50.919
The Princess is not only
building the future of Neo Xianglong,

00:11:51.044 --> 00:11:54.589
but a new order as well,
by forming a coalition

00:11:54.839 --> 00:11:57.008
with the other absolute-defense cities.

00:11:58.509 --> 00:11:59.802
But there are some factions

00:11:59.886 --> 00:12:02.805
that oppose her and prefer
that the world remain as it is.

00:12:03.723 --> 00:12:06.559
Do you mean that those factions
are cooperating with Gold?

00:12:07.477 --> 00:12:12.065
Possibly. But I don't think they could've
created the Dark Drive so easily.

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:14.901
I hate to admit it, but...

00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:17.111
Leon, you are a genius.

00:12:18.196 --> 00:12:21.240
Unless they had an intellectual capacity
rivaling yours,

00:12:21.449 --> 00:12:22.909
they couldn't have made it.

00:12:23.409 --> 00:12:24.744
The only one who could...

00:12:33.795 --> 00:12:35.004
<i>What are you doing?</i>

00:12:35.171 --> 00:12:36.673
Waiting for Leon.

00:12:37.131 --> 00:12:39.258
I heard he went somewhere with Jay.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.427
Do you have plans or something?

00:12:43.554 --> 00:12:45.348
I see. So it's a date?

00:12:45.682 --> 00:12:47.767
What? That's not it!

00:12:47.976 --> 00:12:48.977
I'm just joking.

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:51.312
I know siblings don't go on dates.

00:12:51.688 --> 00:12:52.730
Have you contacted him?

00:12:53.856 --> 00:12:55.566
I know he won't answer if I do,

00:12:55.858 --> 00:12:58.861
and Leon's not the type
to contact me either.

00:12:59.654 --> 00:13:01.906
He may head straight back to our quarters.

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:04.242
He left in the middle of work.

00:13:04.659 --> 00:13:07.787
Whenever he does that,
he always come back to the base.

00:13:08.371 --> 00:13:09.372
I see.

00:13:09.998 --> 00:13:12.959
But if it gets too late,
just return home, okay?

00:13:13.501 --> 00:13:15.128
Well then, take care.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.422
I will. Thanks.

00:13:19.841 --> 00:13:20.842
<i>Dr. Lon...</i>

00:13:21.676 --> 00:13:24.470
<i>Leon, you were always with Dr. Lon.</i>

00:13:25.304 --> 00:13:27.557
<i>He must have acknowledged your intellect.</i>

00:13:29.183 --> 00:13:30.977
If he is still alive...

00:13:31.936 --> 00:13:33.271
That is not possible.

00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:36.232
We've also confirmed
that it was the doctor's corpse.

00:13:36.691 --> 00:13:37.775
However,

00:13:38.109 --> 00:13:40.028
I intend to investigate him further.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:43.573
I need you to tell me everything you know.

00:13:46.325 --> 00:13:47.326
What is it?

00:13:49.203 --> 00:13:50.747
When Dr. Lon died,

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:53.082
there was another person here.

00:13:53.458 --> 00:13:54.959
What? Who?

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:56.753
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:13:57.003 --> 00:13:59.922
<i>Just as I told you before,</i>
<i>I know nothing.</i>

00:14:02.091 --> 00:14:04.969
As I continued the research,
I realized something.

00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:08.890
That the reactor not only acquired energy
from multiple dimensions,

00:14:09.348 --> 00:14:11.934
but that there was a chance
it would affect evolution.

00:14:13.561 --> 00:14:15.438
I understand your apprehension.

00:14:16.064 --> 00:14:21.444
That's why I've only given
reactor core access to you and myself.

00:14:22.028 --> 00:14:23.196
<i>And if we can't</i>

00:14:23.279 --> 00:14:27.200
<i>contain the evolution field that</i>
<i>spills out of the multiple dimensions?</i>

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.660
There'll be a giant Cambrian explosion.

00:14:30.953 --> 00:14:35.708
<i>The few dozen species of organisms</i>
<i>that existed 550 million years ago</i>

00:14:36.209 --> 00:14:39.504
<i>suddenly underwent explosive growth</i>
<i>until there were tens of thousands.</i>

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:42.799
<i>Some species died out, while some evolved.</i>

00:14:43.299 --> 00:14:46.636
<i>The earth transformed</i>
<i>into a giant laboratory of life.</i>

00:14:47.428 --> 00:14:50.431
That kind of change may occur once again.

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:54.560
If it were up to you,
which would you choose?

00:14:55.436 --> 00:14:58.523
Continue research
that could possibly change the world?

00:14:59.023 --> 00:15:00.566
Or stop here?

00:15:02.402 --> 00:15:07.532
Let me introduce you to my assistant
and the chief of my research team.

00:15:07.907 --> 00:15:09.033
Nice to meet you.

00:15:10.451 --> 00:15:11.577
I'm Leon Lau.

00:15:18.501 --> 00:15:21.671
We've received information
from an anonymous source.

00:15:22.213 --> 00:15:23.339
It was you, wasn't it?

00:15:24.382 --> 00:15:25.216
Is it true?

00:15:26.217 --> 00:15:28.928
Is there really something dangerous
about the reactor?

00:15:30.763 --> 00:15:33.182
Cecile had a lot of questions for me.

00:15:34.225 --> 00:15:35.852
So, is that your answer?

00:15:36.602 --> 00:15:39.063
So instead of deciding for yourself

00:15:39.564 --> 00:15:43.067
whether to continue or not,
you left the decision to someone else.

00:15:43.734 --> 00:15:45.361
That's what it boils down to.

00:15:46.028 --> 00:15:48.614
That's the easy way out, Leon.

00:15:48.948 --> 00:15:51.868
It's a decision not to be made lightly.

00:15:52.243 --> 00:15:54.912
I've given you many choices

00:15:55.621 --> 00:15:58.249
in research, entertainment, and sports.

00:15:58.916 --> 00:16:02.587
I came here to observe
the decision you'd made,

00:16:03.129 --> 00:16:05.381
just to find you hadn't made one at all.

00:16:06.883 --> 00:16:09.594
Even without you,
I could have completed the reactor.

00:16:10.136 --> 00:16:12.054
"Then why did you recruit me?"

00:16:13.014 --> 00:16:15.850
I was just curious about you as a person.

00:16:16.392 --> 00:16:19.395
That's why I kept giving you choices
and observed you.

00:16:20.521 --> 00:16:24.942
I thought maybe you could be
someone to explore a new era with me.

00:16:27.445 --> 00:16:29.322
I'm a little disappointed.

00:16:30.281 --> 00:16:32.158
Reactor output is spiking!

00:16:32.241 --> 00:16:33.201
What happened?

00:16:33.284 --> 00:16:34.577
Dr. Lon is inside!

00:16:36.871 --> 00:16:38.247
What are you doing?!

00:16:39.749 --> 00:16:43.961
Once upon a time,
there was a cat who wore glasses.

00:16:44.045 --> 00:16:45.671
His name was Leon.

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:47.173
Meow!

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:52.178
How long do you plan on staying a cat?

00:16:52.929 --> 00:16:56.557
Don't you want to come out of the box
and become the observer?

00:16:56.933 --> 00:16:58.976
Why bring up Schrödinger's cat?

00:16:59.477 --> 00:17:00.853
I'll let you choose again.

00:17:01.687 --> 00:17:04.690
Do you want to continue to raise
the reactor output or not?

00:17:04.982 --> 00:17:07.610
Don't you want to see a new world?

00:17:10.863 --> 00:17:13.616
You neither agree nor disagree.

00:17:13.824 --> 00:17:15.785
That is your weakness.

00:17:16.661 --> 00:17:18.204
I'm disappointed once again.

00:17:18.829 --> 00:17:21.832
If you had stopped me,
this may have never happened.

00:17:22.208 --> 00:17:24.168
This is the result of your choice!

00:17:24.627 --> 00:17:25.836
No! Lon!

00:17:38.474 --> 00:17:39.642
Lo...

00:17:40.226 --> 00:17:41.143
Lon!

00:17:41.561 --> 00:17:42.687
Lon!

00:17:43.479 --> 00:17:44.355
It can't be...

00:18:05.334 --> 00:18:07.461
So, he killed Dr. Lon,

00:18:07.712 --> 00:18:11.674
stole whatever data that was,
and developed the Dark Drive?

00:18:12.216 --> 00:18:13.718
It's a possibility.

00:18:13.801 --> 00:18:17.597
And why didn't you tell us
that it was Dr. Lon

00:18:18.055 --> 00:18:19.473
who overloaded the reactor?

00:18:20.182 --> 00:18:22.393
I didn't want a certain person to know.

00:18:23.102 --> 00:18:26.897
Can you keep what happened
a secret a little longer

00:18:27.064 --> 00:18:29.650
until the truth is clear?

00:18:31.319 --> 00:18:32.862
I suppose that is fine. However,

00:18:32.987 --> 00:18:34.947
I will have to let the Princess know.

00:18:35.197 --> 00:18:37.283
Okay. Thank you.

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:38.826
But...

00:18:39.118 --> 00:18:43.289
who's the person you don't want
finding this out?

00:18:48.669 --> 00:18:50.546
Jeez, you're late!

00:18:51.005 --> 00:18:52.089
I'm sorry.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:54.467
Just kidding. You were working, right?

00:18:55.134 --> 00:18:56.093
Let's get moving.

00:18:56.469 --> 00:18:57.470
Yeah.

00:18:59.305 --> 00:19:02.266
<i>Come to think of it,</i>
<i>I'm surprised you made it back alone.</i>

00:19:02.475 --> 00:19:03.976
<i>I guess you remember the way now.</i>

00:19:04.352 --> 00:19:06.729
Actually, I got a little lost.

00:19:07.605 --> 00:19:08.731
I should've known.

00:19:09.148 --> 00:19:10.733
And then... this way?

00:19:13.194 --> 00:19:16.030
<i>The shop I always bought mahua from</i>
<i>closed down.</i>

00:19:16.739 --> 00:19:19.408
But don't worry.
I found another one that sells them.

00:19:19.659 --> 00:19:21.911
They're smaller than the old ones though.

00:19:23.788 --> 00:19:25.414
<i>We're here! This way!</i>

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:27.625
<i>This was built two years ago.</i>

00:19:28.334 --> 00:19:31.379
<i>It's a memorial for the people who died</i>
<i>in the reactor incident.</i>

00:19:42.348 --> 00:19:43.349
Excuse me.

00:19:45.017 --> 00:19:46.060
What is it?

00:19:46.435 --> 00:19:50.606
It was my sister. School's out right now
and she's in town.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.566
I'll introduce you sometime.

00:19:53.526 --> 00:19:54.527
Her name is Chloe.

00:20:03.869 --> 00:20:05.538
Lon! Lon!

00:20:06.288 --> 00:20:07.206
Lon!

00:20:07.707 --> 00:20:08.916
Lon!

00:20:15.548 --> 00:20:18.634
Lon! Big brother...

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:20.720
Um...

00:20:26.851 --> 00:20:28.102
Here it is!

00:20:28.769 --> 00:20:30.479
I've finally come to see you...

00:20:31.605 --> 00:20:32.606
Big brother.

00:20:35.234 --> 00:20:37.987
I'm doing fine, so please don't worry.

00:20:38.696 --> 00:20:41.407
Can you believe
that I'm living with someone

00:20:41.741 --> 00:20:43.200
you used to do research with?

00:20:44.577 --> 00:20:47.663
You know, maybe it was Lon
who brought us together!

00:20:48.664 --> 00:20:51.208
Ah, yeah...
You may be right.

00:20:51.417 --> 00:20:52.418
What's wrong?

00:20:52.501 --> 00:20:53.627
Nothing.

00:20:54.587 --> 00:20:57.590
It's just... How's life in Neo Xianglong?

00:21:00.009 --> 00:21:01.218
<i>I'm used to it now!</i>

00:21:01.677 --> 00:21:02.928
<i>I enjoy my job, too.</i>

00:21:03.471 --> 00:21:04.680
<i>I see.</i>

00:21:05.514 --> 00:21:06.849
<i>In the past,</i>

00:21:07.099 --> 00:21:09.351
<i>I really was a useless person.</i>

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:12.897
<i>I thought there was no point in things</i>

00:21:13.355 --> 00:21:15.900
<i>like idle chat or making friends.</i>

00:21:17.443 --> 00:21:20.946
<i>But after meeting Lon,</i>
<i>my way of thinking changed.</i>

00:21:21.614 --> 00:21:23.491
<i>I've learned a lot from you too,</i>
<i>Chloe.</i>

00:21:24.033 --> 00:21:27.286
<i>You're both like teachers to me.</i>

00:21:28.329 --> 00:21:30.122
That's why...

00:21:32.666 --> 00:21:35.002
I will continue to protect you,
no matter what!

00:21:40.758 --> 00:21:43.135
Article 37 of the Family Contract.

00:21:43.427 --> 00:21:45.387
"No treating each other like strangers."

00:21:46.055 --> 00:21:49.517
Both you and Lon
are my older brothers after all.

00:22:04.615 --> 00:22:07.827
You who have lost, rejoice.

00:22:08.619 --> 00:22:11.288
I will provide a vent

00:22:11.956 --> 00:22:14.667
for your centuries of resentment.

00:23:46.759 --> 00:23:49.303
THE RED DEATH REAPER

00:23:49.386 --> 00:23:50.929
Subtitle translation by Amanda Miller
